; Mail authentication records for the staging environment, per ADR-0307.
; Placeholders are in angle brackets, such as `<egress-ip>`. Each one is environment-specific.

; The submission agent's own name. It must match maddy's HELO name and the PTR
; record of the dedicated egress IP. Receivers check all three against each other.
mail.staging.example.com.                     IN  A     <egress-ip>

; SPF authorises exactly one sender for this subdomain: the egress IP that maddy
; sends from. Use `-all`, not `~all`. A soft fail asks receivers to accept mail
; that this platform did not send. That is the opposite of the record's purpose.
mail.staging.example.com.                     IN  TXT   "v=spf1 ip4:<egress-ip> -all"

; The DKIM public half. Its private half is in the environment's SopsSecret as
; `maddy-dkim`. The two are generated together, and neither is useful alone.
default._domainkey.mail.staging.example.com.  IN  TXT   "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=<dkim-public-key>"

; DMARC is published ONCE at the organisation domain. It governs the mail
; subdomain through `sp=`, so platform mail and human mail report to one place.
; Keep `p=none` until the aggregate reports are clean. An environment does not
; count as production until this reads `p=reject`.
_dmarc.staging.example.com.                   IN  TXT   "v=DMARC1; p=none; sp=none; fo=1; rua=mailto:dmarc@staging.example.com"
